window.__finlexDocLoaded(10057,{"id":10057,"articles":[{"id":1000278,"no":"Overview","heading":"Official Overview & Scope (IFRS Foundation)","text":"Superseded by IFRS 9 Financial Instruments.\n\nIFRIC 9 clarifies that an entity must assess whether an embedded derivative is required by IAS 39 to be separated from the host contract and accounted for as a derivative when the entity first becomes a party to the contract.\n\nSubsequent reassessment is prohibited unless there is a change in the terms of the contract that significantly modifies the cash flows that otherwise would be required under the contract, in which case reassessment is required. A first-time adopter must assess whether an embedded derivative is required to be separated on the basis of the conditions that existed at the date it first became a party to the contract, unless there was a subsequent change in terms of the contract that significantly modified the cash flows.","seq":0},{"id":1000279,"no":"History","heading":"Standard History & Amendments","text":"In March 2006, the International Accounting Standards Board (IASB) issued IFRIC 9 Reassessment of Embedded Derivatives.\n\nIt was developed by the Interpretations Committee. Other Standards have made minor consequential amendments to IFRIC 9, including IFRS 11 Joint Arrangements (issued May 2011).\n\nIFRIC 9 was superseded by IFRS 9 Financial Instruments.","seq":1},{"id":1000280,"no":"Support","heading":"Related Projects & Implementation Support","text":"[Related active projects]\n[Related completed projects]\nEmbedded Derivatives (Amendments to IFRIC 9 and IAS 39)\n[Related IFRS Standards]\nIAS 39 Financial Instruments: Recognition and Measurement\nIFRS 9 Financial Instruments\n[Related IFRIC Interpretations]\n[Unconsolidated amendments]\n[Implementation support]","seq":2},{"id":1000281,"no":"References","heading":"Official Text Link & Public Practical Guidance","text":"Official IFRS Foundation Page (English): https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/ifric-9-reassessment-of-embedded-derivatives/\nAccess Note: Free access to the unaccompanied text of IFRS Accounting Standards on ifrs.org requires a free registered IFRS.org account; Basis for Conclusions and Illustrative Examples require an IFRS Digital Subscription.\nPublic Companion Overview: KPMG Insights into IFRS — An Overview (Sept 2026): https://assets.kpmg.com/content/dam/kpmgsites/xx/pdf/ifrg/2026/isg-2026-insights-an-overview.pdf","seq":3}]});
